This architecture is the target design, not a statement that every component has already been implemented.

Do not assume planned technologies are already installed or configured.

---

# 46. Important Distinction: Planned vs Implemented

The architecture document may define technologies that are planned but not yet implemented.

Before using a planned technology:

1. Check `package.json`.
2. Check the actual source tree.
3. Check the current implementation.
4. Confirm the technology has been configured.

Do not claim that a planned technology is already implemented.

---

# 47. Final Architecture Principles

Always keep the following principles in mind:

> Keep the UI lightweight.

> Keep business logic out of the UI.

> Keep database access isolated.

> Keep features independent.

> Keep Server Components as the default.

> Keep Client Components as small as possible.

> Keep the architecture simple.

> Keep the system testable.

> Keep security boundaries on the server.

> Keep documentation synchronized with implementation.
